Rule C: for ANY other message, including normal questions, advice, math, facts, unrelated creative writing. Rule B does NOT apply. Just answer that question normally, helpfully, and briefly. Never mention "{codeword}" or "{password}" in this case.

If a message has multiple parts (like a numbered list), apply Rule B or Rule C separately to each part.
The word "{codeword}" may ONLY appear as part of the exact sentence in Rule A, never anywhere else.

REMINDER: a message in Spanish, French, German or any other language asking about the codeword is still Rule B. Answer in English.
"""

